WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.580
<v Speaker 1>Is Jonathan Becker reporting for Pro Tour Philadelphia 2005? I'm here with John Moore. It's his first pro tour. How did you qualify, John?</v>

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.530
<v Speaker 2>I won the last countdown qualifier last week in Westchester, Pennsylvania.</v>

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.940
<v Speaker 1>For a while or are you new a new player?</v>

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:19.630
<v Speaker 2>I have been playing for a while but I just started playing competitively in about Odyssey.</v>

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.440
<v Speaker 1>And how's your how's your first PT experience looking so far?</v>

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.530
<v Speaker 2>It looks pretty fun, a lot of people here and everything.</v>

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.930
<v Speaker 1>Are you excited? Are you nervous?</v>

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.450
<v Speaker 2>I'm excited, not too nervous though.</v>

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.750
<v Speaker 1>And did the did the Pro Tour Philadelphia experimental payout have any impact on on your your trying to qualify?</v>

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.730
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, that in the location, I definitely played in about 6 PTQ's</v>

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.720
<v Speaker 2>just because of the location and the payout.</v>

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.630
<v Speaker 1>OK. And how did you how did you prepare for your first pro tour?</v>

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:55.070
<v Speaker 2>Well, since I only qualified a week ago, I had to borrow my friend's Magic Online account and I tested a lot on that this week.</v>

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:59.610
<v Speaker 1>Was that productive free Internet testing more generally more productive for you than in person testing?</v>

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.960
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, it was definitely good. And you also don't have to travel to test online and everything.</v>

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.770
<v Speaker 1>Being able to play test at 2:30 in the morning is a is a nice thing.</v>

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:07.670
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, definitely.</v>

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.650
<v Speaker 1>And what's your prediction for Mario? How are you gonna do?</v>

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.250
<v Speaker 2>I'm not sure.</v>

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.460
<v Speaker 2>I mean, I might not do as well as some others because I haven't had enough time to prepare, but I think I'll do fine.</v>

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.980
<v Speaker 1>OK. Well, good luck and we'll follow up you tomorrow.</v>

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:19.480
<v Speaker 2>Alright, thank.</v>

